  "term": "DTD",
  "definition": "DTD stands for difficult-to-treat depression, a broad term for depressive conditions that still cause major problems despite usual treatment. It describes suboptimal results related to treatment failure, including lack of response, intolerance, non-acceptance, or contraindications across treatment options.",
